                <head>ETA–16. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>On January 7, 1959, Acting Secretary Dillon approved a request contained in a memorandum from
                    Assistant Secretary Mann, dated January
                    5, for authority to negotiate and draft an agreement with representatives of the
                    other American Republics for the establishment of an inter-American development
                    institution. A copy of the memorandum, with the Under Secretary’s hand-written
                    authorization is filed under decimal number 810.10/1–559.</p>
            </div>
